// Title: Forfiles.EXE Child Process Masquerading
// ID: f53714ec-5077-420e-ad20-907ff9bb2958
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), Anish Bogati
// Date: 2024-01-05
// Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1036
// Description: Detects the execution of "forfiles" from a non-default location, in order to potentially spawn a custom "cmd.exe" from the current working directory.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where (((process.parent.command_line endswith ".exe" or process.parent.command_line endswith ".exe\"") and process.executable endswith "\\cmd.exe" and process.command_line startswith "/c echo \"") and not (((process.parent.executable like "*_:\\Windows\\System32\\*" or process.parent.executable like "*_:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\*") and process.parent.executable endswith "\\forfiles.exe" and (process.executable like "*_:\\Windows\\System32\\*" or process.executable like "*_:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\*") and process.executable endswith "\\cmd.exe")))
